\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Evaluation protocol and pair counts for each dataset split. Writer counts refer to the train, validation, and test partitions. For each partition, the number of genuine and impostor pairs is equal, corresponding to the 50\% positive-ratio setting. Genuine pairs are fixed, whereas impostor pairs are sampled from a larger candidate pool and resampled every epoch. The same pair-generation procedure is used across all backbone/loss configurations, so pair counts are identical across the 18 configurations within each split.}}{10}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
